      "name": "Gun Safe Move Operations",
      "description": "Gun safe and high-mass safe moving under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol, for safes of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs. The published operation chain runs quote intake (make, model, or approximate weight; pickup and delivery addresses; access at both ends) to route and clearance survey, floor deflection analysis to L/360 with a load-spreading plan, floor protection, controlled move, secured upright transport, and verified placement exactly where the owner wants it, quoted at one flat rate in writing before move day. The protocol page states the same five steps in order: survey and floor check, protect and move, place and verify. Quote intake runs through the Short (Quick Quote) default and Detailed Project toggle, inputs preserved, and a film-only video walkthrough where a walkthrough fits: film only, never lift, move, open, or climb anything heavy or locked, with a human-made estimate. Published service practice: safes under 1,500 lbs handled the same careful way; the safe is emptied first, always; stairs go up and down; equipment matched to the project; re-anchoring at the destination available on request; vault work covers any size; standard safe classes; no locksmith services. Published long-distance safe runs include Winchester to Las Vegas; long-distance research covers high-value items and demographics as audience depth. Full per-topic detail is in the ten service-detail nodes appended to this file.",
